sequenceDiagram
  participant Browser
  participant API
  participant DB
  Browser->>API: POST registration (terms accepted, optional marketing consent)
  API->>DB: create pending_approval user and customer role
  opt Marketing consent selected
    API->>DB: create newsletter subscription
  end
  API-->>Browser: 202 email verification required (no session)
  API->>Browser: signed email verification link
  Browser->>API: GET signed verification link
  API->>DB: mark email verified
  API-->>Browser: redirect to pending approval page
  Browser->>API: POST staff invitation token and password
  API->>DB: lock one-time invite, create active verified user and role
  API-->>Browser: invitation accepted
Browser->>API: POST login (email or phone for Storefront; optional remember_me; email for Admin)
  API->>DB: verify user and roles
  alt Admin has 2FA enabled
    API->>DB: look up hashed trusted-device cookie
    alt Trusted device valid
      API->>DB: rotate trusted-device hash and extend expiry
      API->>DB: create revocable session row
      API-->>Browser: signed JWT + refresh cookie + rotated trusted-device cookie
    else Device needs verification
      API->>DB: store short-lived hashed challenge
      API-->>Browser: 202 challenge token (memory only)
      Browser->>API: POST TOTP or recovery code (optional trust for 30 days)
      API->>DB: lock challenge, verify code, consume challenge and recovery code
      opt Trust this device
        API->>DB: store trusted-device token hash
      end
      API->>DB: create revocable session row
      API-->>Browser: signed JWT + httpOnly refresh cookie (and optional trusted-device cookie)
    end
  else 2FA not enabled
  API->>DB: create revocable session row
  API-->>Browser: signed 15-minute JWT (aud, sid) + httpOnly refresh cookie (session-only unless remembered)
  end
  Browser->>API: Bearer access token
  API-->>Browser: protected response
  API-->>Browser: 401 when access token expires
  Browser->>API: one shared POST refresh for concurrent requests (cookie)
  API->>DB: lock refresh row and validate hash/audience
  alt Token was already revoked
    API->>DB: follow replaced_by_id chain; revoke family refresh and access sessions
    API-->>Browser: 401 + clear audience cookie
  else Token is current and valid
    API->>DB: rotate refresh cookie and issue new JWT in one transaction
    API-->>Browser: signed JWT + rotated httpOnly cookie preserving the original session/persistent choice
  end
  Browser->>API: retry each failed request once with new token
  alt Storefront refresh rejected with 401/419
    Browser->>Browser: clear in-memory access token
    Browser->>Browser: navigate to login with expired notice and safe returnTo
    Browser->>API: POST storefront login credentials
    API->>DB: create new storefront session and rotate refresh cookie
    API-->>Browser: restore access token and resume returnTo route
  else Admin refresh fails or retried request is unauthorized
    API-->>Browser: keep route mounted and require password
    Browser->>API: POST admin login credentials
    alt Admin has 2FA enabled
      API-->>Browser: 202 short-lived challenge
      Browser->>API: POST TOTP or recovery code
    end
    API->>DB: create a new revocable session and rotate refresh cookie
    API-->>Browser: restore access token and resume current route
  end
  Browser->>API: PUT account email with current password
  API->>DB: store pending address and token hash with expiry
  API->>Browser: queue confirmation link to new address
  Browser->>API: GET one-time email change token
  API->>DB: verify hash and expiry; replace account email atomically
  API->>DB: delete consumed pending request
  API->>Browser: notify previous address and redirect to account security
  API->>Browser: redirect to account security
  Browser->>API: POST account phone change (recent auth + current password)
  API->>DB: store one pending phone and HMAC of six-digit code
  API->>Browser: send SMS code; return masked phone and expiry
  Browser->>API: POST phone change confirmation
  API->>DB: lock challenge; check expiry/attempts/code; replace phone and set verified timestamp
  Browser->>API: POST login by phone
  API->>DB: reject phone login unless phone_verified_at is set
